      "preview": "**\ud83e\udd4a Tale of the Tape:**  \nnoahsaint\u2019s 8\u20111 engine is built on a balanced attack\u2014Purdy\u2019s efficient passing paired with a three\u2011back committee that maximizes carry volume. Mr\u202ftexas\u202fis scrambling for relevance, leaning on a volatile Dak\u2011Prescott combo and a run\u2011heavy backfield that lacks a clear lead\u2011back cadence.\n\n**\ud83d\udd25 The X\u2011Factors:**  \n- **noahsaint:** Brock\u202fPurdy (SF) is entering Week\u202f10 with a 7.2\u202fYPA average and 45\u202f% rushing upside, facing a secondary that ranks in the bottom\u2011quartile against QBs who scramble. Rhamondre\u202fStevenson (NE) continues to command >18\u202fcarries per game against a run defense that allows 4.9\u202fYPC, guaranteeing a solid floor. Jaxon\u202fSmith\u2011Njigba (SEA) is the primary slot target on a route\u2011tree that sees >6\u202ftargets per game, translating to a high ceiling in a matchup versus a 3rd\u2011ranked pass\u2011defense.\n\n- **Mr texas :** Dak\u202fPrescott (DAL) is the only true dual\u2011threat starter; he averages 6.1\u202fYPA and adds 3.2\u202frush\u202fYPG, but he now faces a top\u201110 pass rush that has sacked QBs 3.8\u00d7 per game, threatening his efficiency. Kenneth\u202fWalker\u202fIII (KC) is the lead back with 19\u202fcarries per game, yet he meets a defensive front that has limited opponents to 3.8\u202fYPC this season, capping upside. The newly\u2011acquired Keenan\u202fAllen (SF) is now on a 49ers offense that spreads the ball, but his target share drops to ~4\u202fper game against a secondary that ranks 2nd in opponent WR efficiency, limiting his impact.\n\n**\ud83d\udd2e The Verdict:**  \nnoahsaint defeats Mr\u202ftexas , 120.8 to 79.1, driven by a multi\u2011dimensional rushing attack that secures high\u2011volume, high\u2011efficiency touches against permissive run defenses while Purdy\u2019s dual\u2011threat profile exploits a vulnerable pass rush."
